# Files in the repo root that should NOT be served as part of the site.
#
# wrangler.jsonc sets `assets.directory` to ".", so by default every file in
# the repository is published, including internal planning documents. Nothing
# here is secret, but docs/PRD.md is an internal roadmap and there is no reason
# for it to have a public URL.
#
# Syntax is gitignore-style. Anything NOT listed here is still served, so the
# pages, css/, js/ and data/ are untouched.

# Internal documentation and planning
docs/
README.md

# Build, test and data-refresh tooling (Python; never executed by the site)
scripts/

# Input to scripts/update_metrics.py, not a site asset. No .html or .js
# references it, and deploy.yml already excluded it from the GitHub Pages build
# without this file being kept in step.
#
# It has to be here, not merely ought to be: on 2026-09-01 a routine metrics
# refresh (90f6dcf) grew it from 22.8 MB past Cloudflare's 25 MiB per-file
# upload limit, which fails the WHOLE deployment. The site stopped updating and
# the only symptom was a red build. scripts/check_asset_sizes.py now catches
# this class of failure before a push.
data/symphony_scores.json

# Local UI mockups: gitignored as well, listed here as a second line of defence
_wf-mockup.html
_harness_*.html
_harness_*_driver.js

# Repo and tooling config.
#
# `.git/` is listed defensively. wrangler may well exclude it already, but a
# build log reported reading 140 files from the assets directory where a clean
# clone holds 91 tracked ones, and the likeliest remainder is the repository
# itself. If it were served, /.git/ would expose the full history and every
# stray file ever committed. One line closes the question either way.
.git/
wrangler.jsonc
.gitignore
.assetsignore
.github/
